The JSON files in this directory are hand-curated summaries of chapters from
the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention's (CDC) "Epidemiology and
Prevention of Vaccine-Preventable Diseases" (the "Pink Book"), 14th Edition,
2021 — a work of the United States federal government.

Unlike data/supportingdata/antigens and data/supportingdata/schedule, these
files are NOT verbatim CDC data. Each summary was written by a contributor
to this project (with AI assistance) by reading the original chapter text
and condensing it into the schema defined in
src/OpenCdsi.ClinicalReference/Models/AntigenChapter.cs. The specific
wording, selection, and organization of each summary is this project's own
work and is covered by the Mozilla Public License 2.0 that applies to the
rest of this repository's source (see the LICENSE file at the repository
root).

The underlying facts and the CDC's original chapter text remain the CDC's
own public-domain work. Works of the United States federal government are
generally not subject to copyright protection within the United States
under 17 U.S.C. § 105. This statement is provided for general information
only and is not legal advice; confirm actual usage terms directly with the
CDC, or with your own counsel, before relying on this content for any
specific distribution or use — especially if you intend to reproduce the
CDC's original chapter text rather than this project's own summaries of it.

Each file's own "source" field names the specific Pink Book edition and the
chapter's canonical CDC URL. These summaries are a snapshot as of that
edition and are not kept in sync with CDC's live, continuously updated Pink
Book website — consult CDC's own publication channels for the current,
authoritative text. See CONTRIBUTING.md in this directory for how this
content was produced and how to refresh it against a future edition.
